     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This order is twice that. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max dose.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is a typical dosing pattern.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and note the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably still flag it."
      }
     ],
